{# repo integration report section (spec repo §9.2).

Renders one repository's structured payload:
- H2: repo name with GitHub link
- failure banner (only when status == "failed"): a ❌ blockquote with the
  failure_reason, so a repo whose diff failed (e.g. a GC'd checkpoint
  'bad object') is not silently rendered as a bare heading
- small badge: 🌿 branch + ✏️ commit count (separate line, like ffd9d3c)
- release block (only when releases present): each release as a <details> block
  with 🚀 title 🏷️ tag summary, notes, AI summary (with fallback) and a nested
  detail block labelled "Click to view detailed release analysis"
- single `---` separator (only when both release AND commit blocks present)
- commit block (only when commits present): truncation warning + commits + analysis

Commit rendering (Feature 2 & 3):
- ``commits`` is a list of {subject, body} dicts. A commit with a non-empty body
  renders as a <details> block (subject in <summary>, body inside); a bodyless
  commit renders as a flat <div>. Squash-duplicated bodies (body == subject) are
  already collapsed to "" by _split_commit_message, so the subject shows once.

HTML escaping rules (security critical):
- commit subject/body MUST be HTML-escaped (external data)
- AI summary/detail are NOT escaped (trusted output, may contain formatted HTML)
#}
